The function works by initializing a 2D array `dp` of size `(m+1) x (n+1)` where `dp[i][j]` represents the length of the longest common subsequence of the first `i` characters of `str1` and the first `j` characters of `str2`. The base cases are `dp[0][0] = 0` and `dp[m][n] = 0`.
The function then iterates through the first `m` characters of `str1` and the first `n` characters of `str2` and updates the value of `dp[i][j]` based on the length of the longest common subsequence of the first `i-1` characters of `str1` and the first `j-1` characters of `str2`.
The function returns the value of `dp[m][n]`, which represents the length of the longest common subsequence of the two input strings.
The bug in the function is that it does not handle the case where `str1` and `str2` are equal. In this case, the function should return 0 instead of `dp[m][n]`
