        return 1
    elif n == 1:
        return 1
    else:
        return count_full_trees(n-1) + count_full_trees(n-2)
```
This function first checks if the number of vertices is 0 or 1, in which case there is only one full binary tree. Otherwise, it recursively calls itself twice, once with n-1 vertices and once with n-2 vertices, and adds the results together.

