4. "Amy" (2015) - Directed by Asif Kapadia, this film tells the story of Amy Winehouse, the British singer-songwriter who died at the age of 27. The film uses a mix of archival footage and interviews to paint a portrait of Winehouse's life and career.
5. "O.J.: Made in America" (2016) - Directed by Ezra Edelman, this film is a comprehensive look at the life and career of O.J. Simpson, as well as the social and political context of the murder trial that captivated the nation in the 1990s. The film won the Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature.

These films are all excellent examples of the power of documentary filmmaking and the impact it can have on society. By studying these films, aspiring filmmakers can learn about the craft of documentary filmmaking, as well as the importance of telling compelling stories that resonate with audiences.
